.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1828.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17057,"officials":[{"fullName":"Dan Kelly","displayName":"Dan Kelly","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Frederick L'Ecuyer","displayName":"Frederick L'Ecuyer","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Mark Shewchyk","displayName":"Mark Shewchyk","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Beau Halkidis","displayName":"Beau Halkidis","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Kent Johnson scores lone goal in shootout to give Blue Jackets 3-2 win over Penguins","description":"— Kent Johnson scored the only goal in a shootout to lift the Columbus Blue Jackets over the Pittsburgh Penguins 3-2 on Friday night.","story":"COLUMBUS, Ohio -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4781553/kent-johnson\">Kent Johnson</a> scored the only goal in a shootout to lift the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/cbj/columbus-blue-jackets\">Columbus Blue Jackets</a> over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/pit/pittsburgh-penguins\">Pittsburgh Penguins</a> 3-2 on Friday night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3068087/damon-severson\">Damon Severson</a> had a goal and an assist for Columbus. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4064781/mathieu-olivier\">Mathieu Olivier</a> also scored, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874725/cole-sillinger\">Cole Sillinger</a> added two assists.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5734/cam-talbot\">Cam Talbot</a> made 20 saves and denied all three Pittsburgh attempts in the shootout. He became <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/cam-talbot-columbus-blue-jackets-cbeadfd9f36dcc3ffe7b44fe43b6a466\">the first NHL goalie to win a game with nine teams.</a>\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3124/evgeni-malkin\">Evgeni Malkin</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2591155/bryan-rust\">Bryan Rust</a> scored for the Penguins, who have dropped three straight games since winning their first two this season. Malkin tied it 2-all at 3:19 of the third period.\n\n\r\n              Johnson beat <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188366/sergei-murashov\">Sergei Murashov</a> with a snap shot to begin the shootout.\n\n\r\n              Murashov stopped 43 shots in regulation.\n\n\r\n              The Blue Jackets outshot the Penguins 45-22 and won 66.7% of the faceoffs. Columbus outhit Pittsburgh 21-9. \n\n\r\n              The Penguins blocked 20 shots.\n\n\r\n              Talbot, in his 13th NHL season, has also won games with the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyr/new-york-rangers\">New York Rangers</a>, Edmonton, Philadelphia, Calgary, Minnesota, Ottawa, Detroit and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/la/los-angeles-kings\">Los Angeles Kings</a>.\n\n\r\n              In his first season with Columbus, he broke the previous record held by Curtis McElhinney, Sean Burke and Ron Tugnutt.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Penguins: Host the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/dal/dallas-stars\">Dallas Stars</a> on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              Blue Jackets: At the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/stl/st-louis-blues\">St. Louis Blues</a> on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              The Associated Press created this story using technology provided by <a href=\"https://www.dataskrive.com/\">Data Skrive</a> and data from <a href=\"https://www.sportradar.com/\">Sportradar</a>.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-10T02:20:27Z"}}